      "text": "Mary and Max is a stop-motion movie that tells the story of a friendship between a little girl, Mary, who lives in Australia and a middle-aged man with Asperger’s syndrome, Max, who lives in New York City. Mary is a neglected child, she feels misunderstood at home. Her mother is an alcoholic and keeps drinking Sherry all day. The beginning of their friendship is a coincidence. Mary just randomly picks a name from a New York phone book and writes a letter, and the guy she writes to is Max. Surprisingly, Max writes her back, and their friendship begins. Through their letters, they share their fears, lives, dreams, and personal struggles, and sometimes they send each other some sweets. They form a deep bond despite their age, and they have never met each other in person."
