      "text": "B1: Stereotyped or repetitive motor movements, use of objects, or speech. Max exhibits a strong preference for the symmetrical arrangement of objects, carefully placing items in a neat, orderly, and balanced manner. This behaviour reflects a form of stereotyped or repetitive use of objects, consistent with Criterion B1 of the DSM-5 diagnostic criteria for Autism Spectrum Disorder. In addition, when replying to Mary’s letters, he often uses a fixed and structured style of language. At times, his letters include peculiar phrases or unique literal interpretations, which further reflect his tendency toward idiosyncratic speech. These behaviours are consistent with the criteria described in B1."
