      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The film American Psycho presents an extreme and complex psychological state derived from a materialistic society through the characterisation of the protagonist, Patrick Bateman, who is a successful, perfect, and admired Wall Street elite on the surface, but in his private life, he hides an extremely violent, cold-blooded, and twisted fantasy side. According to the DSM-V's diagnostic criteria, Bateman's behaviour and performance in the film are highly consistent with the symptoms of Antisocial Personality Disorder (ASPD), Narcissistic Personality Disorder (NPD), Obsessive-Compulsive Personality Disorder (OCPD), as well as delusions and hallucinations in the latter part of the film, suggesting that he may have psychotic features or dissociative symptoms as well."
