      "text": "Same as Susanna, Lisa Rowe’s personality disorder also falls into cluster B of the personality disorders, which are characterised by dramatic, erratic, and emotionally intense behaviours. To be specific, Lisa is diagnosed with Antisocial Personality Disorder (ASPD) and has shown a pervasive pattern of disregard for and violation of the rights of others. Lisa’s character is very well portrayed through the movie, clearly showing the characteristics of ASPD patients and revealing the struggles behind their behaviours and language. However, this research will still examine her portrayal through the description of DSM-5. First, Lisa shows failure to conform to social norms. She is repeatedly breaking rules and escaping from the psychiatric hospital. She doesn’t follow the rules of the hospital, especially, she refuses to take medicine and sneaks into the doctor’s office to read different documentation. Moreover, according to Lisa’s depiction, she aligns with the symptoms of deception in the diagnostic Criterion A of ASPD. She frequently lies and manipulates others; her deceptive behaviour is primarily for personal fulfilment of power and entertainment. Furthermore, Lisa shows impulsivity through the movie. Her escape attempts are unplanned and reckless. She loves escapes without knowing where she will go, and her decisions often seem driven by her impulsivity and emotions instead of a specific goal or plan."
