      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ti West’s Pearl (2022) in his X series presents a psychologically rich and disturbing portrait of Pearl, who is internally fragile yet violent. Through the film’s stylised narrative and emphasis on the characters’ psychological activity to illustrate a combination of ASPD, NPD and symptoms of Brief Psychotic Disorder in Pearl. Pearl’s portrait is clinically resonant with the description in the DSM-5, however, the film intensified several traits in Pearl’s disorder and reveals multiple stereotypes that may mislead audiences’ perceptions toward mental health."
